Experiment - 5(b): Write a shell script that takes file names as arguments and convert all of them to uppercase.

Steps to follow:-
(i) Open the terminal in Ubuntu.
(ii) Create a shell script :- nano upper.sh
(iii) Enter the following code:-
#!/bin/bash
for file in "$@"
do
mv "$file" "$(echo "$file" | tr '[:lower:]' '[:upper:]')"
done
(iv) Save the file using Ctrl + O, press Enter, then Ctrl + X.
(v) Give Execute permission :- chmod + x upper.sh
(vi) Create some sample files :- touch apple.txt banana.txt
(vii) Execute the script by passing file names as command-line arguments:-
./upper.sh apple.txt banana.txt
(viii) Check the result :- ls.
(ix) The file should now appear as :- APPLE.TXT
                                      BANANA.TXT

Result:
Successfully created and executed a shell script that converts the given file names to uppercase.
